.TH travesty 6.SH NAMEtravesty \- make a travesty of the input.SH SYNTAXtravesty[\fB\-n\fInum] [\fB\-o\fIord] [\fB\-r\fIrand] [\fB\-sS\fI] [\fB\-ACHUVW\fI].SH DESCRIPTION.I travestymakes a travesty of its input:it outputs a random stream of characters bya Markov process of some order with frequenciestaken from the input text. In other words,it produces output with the same distribution as the inputof letters, pairs of letters, and so on upto the order..PPThis implementation of.I travestyis very, very fast.For an order.I ordprocess on an input file of length.I len,it uses approximately.I ord*lenspace,.I ord*lentime to read and process the input,and at most.I ord*\fBlog\fI(len)time for each output character.As it produces more output it becomes even more efficient;after a while it produces each character in constant time!.PPOptions.B ACHUVWprint the authorship notice,copyright notice,help notice,short usage summary,version number,and warranty information respectively..PP.I travestyhas a few flags:.TP 12\fB\-n\fInumOutput.I numcharacters (default 0, meaning forever).Remember that this.I travestyis very fast:you can't just watch characters pop up one by one..TP\fB\-o\fIordUse a process of order.I ord;in other words, choose each character based on the.I ordcharacters preceding it.High orders (15 or so) almost always just reproduce the input text.Orders 3 through 8 seem to be the most interesting,depending on the size of the input.The default order is 5..TP\fB\-s\fIStart the output with the same characters as the input..TP\fB\-S\fIStart the output at a random spot in the input (default).Note that.I travestytakes the input text to bewrapped around from the end to the beginning..TP\fB\-r\fIrandSet a particular integer seed for the random number generator.If you do not specify.I\-r,.I travestywill choose a seed based on the current time.It will print the seed on standard error if itreceives an ALRM signal..PP.SH DIAGNOSTICS.TP.I fatal: input too big.I travestydoes not have enough memory to handle the input..SH RESTRICTIONS.I travestycannot deal with ridiculously high ordersor inputs that cannot fit into memory..SH BUGSNone known..SH MACHINES.I travestyhas been testedon an Astronautics ZS-2 running ZSUnix..SH VERSIONtravesty version 1.1, dated 12/23/89..SH AUTHORCopyright 1989, Daniel J. Bernstein..SH "SEE ALSO"kill(1)